cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Ostler, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Ostler: an MCP browser for AI agents that reads, researches and acts, and checks its own work"
abstract: >-
  Ostler is an open-source MCP browser for AI coding agents such as Claude Code,
  Codex and Cursor. It reads, researches and acts in a real Chrome, and checks
  its own work: research answers cite only pages it actually read, with every
  quote verified; forms are filled in one call with every value read back; and
  Qdrant remembers what worked.
authors:
  - family-names: Inamdar
    given-names: Mihir
version: 0.2.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/inamdarmihir/ostler"
url: "https://inamdarmihir.github.io/ostler/"
keywords:
  - mcp
  - model context protocol
  - browser automation
  - ai agents
  - deep research
  - citation verification
  - form filling
  - qdrant
